{red|What are the significant wounds you carry from past relationships?}

This could include betrayal, abandonment, rejection, emotional abuse, being cheated on, having your trust broken, not feeling chosen, or any other relational pain.

Be specific. Name them. They lose some power when brought into the light.

{red|How has your past relationship experience affected your trust in yourself?}

{red|Do you doubt your judgment? Question your ability to read people? Second-guess your perceptions?}

Describe specifically how your self-trust was damaged.

Based on your past relationships, what has your sense of "normal" been?

{red|Have you confused intensity with connection? Drama with passion? Chaos with chemistry?}

{red|What might need to be recalibrated?}

{red|What walls have you built to protect yourself? How do they show up?}

{red|Do you avoid getting close? End things before they can hurt you? Test people excessively? Withhold your true self?}

Be specific about your protective patterns.

{red|Where do you tend to fall on the spectrum?}

Too walled off (keeping everyone at distance)?
Too open (giving access too quickly, not protecting yourself)?

{red|What would it look like for you to move toward healthy balance?}
